hip-virtual-mem: a commit of intel/llvm that v7.2.0 does not have, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.
upstream commit: c13ad6c7e3899094734cd664dfcabc069256bf96

It is intel/llvm's c13ad6c7e3899094734cd664dfcabc069256bf96, "[UR][HIP] Implement virtual and physical
memory management" (pull request 22671, 2026-08-03), as it is: the commit's diff without a change, which
applies to v7.2.0 with the patches before this one.  This patch goes when intel/llvm is raised to a release
that has the commit.

v7.2.0's HIP adapter answered every virtual memory call (urVirtualMem*, urPhysicalMem*) with
UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE and reported no virtual memory support, so SYCL's ext_oneapi_virtual_mem was not there
on AMD GPUs: XeStrata's --vram-elastic (the expert cache in segments it gives back for an image job and maps
again after it) and the elastic K/V (--kv-grow) fell back to one allocation.  The commit implements the calls
with HIP's virtual memory management (hipMemAddressReserve, hipMemCreate, hipMemMap, hipMemSetAccess and the
others), as the CUDA adapter implements them with CUDA's, and the device reports the support HIP's
hipDeviceAttributeVirtualMemoryManagementSupported says it has.

XeStrata's changes to it are patches of their own, after this one: hip-virtual-mem-unmap,
hip-virtual-mem-release and hip-physical-mem-device.
---
diff --git a/sycl/test-e2e/VirtualMem/vector_with_virtual_mem.cpp b/sycl/test-e2e/VirtualMem/vector_with_virtual_mem.cpp
index 154932d719ba6..05959a0e0fecd 100644
--- a/sycl/test-e2e/VirtualMem/vector_with_virtual_mem.cpp
+++ b/sycl/test-e2e/VirtualMem/vector_with_virtual_mem.cpp
@@ -188,13 +188,14 @@ int main() {
     // Copy back the values and verify.
     int *CopyBack = sycl::malloc_shared<int>(NewVecSize, Q);
 
-    // TODO: Level-zero (excluding on PVC) does not currently allow copy across
-    //       virtual memory ranges, even if they are consequtive.
+    // TODO: Level-zero (excluding on PVC) and HIP do not currently allow copy
+    //       across virtual memory ranges, even if they are consequtive.
     syclext::architecture DevArch =
         Q.get_device().get_info<syclext::info::device::architecture>();
-    if (Q.get_backend() == sycl::backend::ext_oneapi_level_zero &&
-        DevArch != syclext::architecture::intel_gpu_pvc &&
-        DevArch != syclext::architecture::intel_gpu_pvc_vg) {
+    if ((Q.get_backend() == sycl::backend::ext_oneapi_level_zero &&
+         DevArch != syclext::architecture::intel_gpu_pvc &&
+         DevArch != syclext::architecture::intel_gpu_pvc_vg) ||
+        Q.get_backend() == sycl::backend::ext_oneapi_hip) {
       Q.parallel_for(sycl::range<1>{NewVecSize}, [=](sycl::id<1> Idx) {
          CopyBack[Idx] = VecDataPtr[Idx];
        }).wait_and_throw();
